// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`describePhase > renders the follicular description 1`] = `
"Days 6–12 of an estimated 28-day cycle.

Estrogen rises as follicles in the ovaries develop, and the uterine lining begins to rebuild.

Commonly reported (everyone is different):
• Energy and motivation building
• A brighter, more social mood
• Feeling focused and open to new things

Estimated from your last 6 cycles.

General information, not medical advice. Not for contraception."
`;

exports[`describePhase > renders the luteal description 1`] = `
"Days 16–28 of an estimated 28-day cycle.

Progesterone rises after ovulation. If pregnancy does not occur, progesterone and estrogen fall toward the end of this phase, leading into the next period.

Commonly reported (everyone is different):
• Steady energy early on, tapering later
• In the final days, PMS for some: bloating, irritability or low mood
• Food cravings
• Lighter or more restless sleep

Estimated from your last 6 cycles.

General information, not medical advice. Not for contraception."
`;

exports[`describePhase > renders the menstrual description 1`] = `
"Days 1–5 of an estimated 28-day cycle.

Estrogen and progesterone are at their lowest, and the uterine lining is shed as a period.

Commonly reported (everyone is different):
• Lower energy, especially in the first few days
• Cramps or lower back ache
• Wanting more rest and quieter time
• Mood often lifting as the period eases

Estimated from your last 6 cycles.

General information, not medical advice. Not for contraception."
`;

exports[`describePhase > renders the ovulatory description 1`] = `
"Days 13–15 of an estimated 28-day cycle.

Estrogen peaks and a surge of luteinizing hormone (LH) triggers the release of an egg. These dates are an estimate: actual ovulation can shift by several days from cycle to cycle, and this calendar cannot detect it.

Commonly reported (everyone is different):
• Peak energy for many people
• Feeling confident and sociable
• Higher libido

Estimated from your last 6 cycles.

General information, not medical advice. Not for contraception."
`;
